W: 2. Straightway unto her love she goes
W: Into his room him to awaken
W: Saying, Arise my love and go away
W: This very night you will be taken
W: I overheard my father say
W: In spite of me he would transport you
W: So arise my love and go away
W: This very night you will be taken
W:
W: 3. Oh must I go, he says to her
W: Oh must I go without my wages
W: Without a penny in my purse
W: Just like some poor forlorn stranger
W: Here’s fifty guineas in bright gold
W: And that’s far more than father owes you
W: So take it now and go away
W: I wish to God I’d gone before you
